    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Basics"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Start with the fundamentals to build a strong foundation:"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "numbered-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "**What is LINQ** — Understand what LINQ is and its purpose",
          "**Why LINQ** — Learn the advantages of LINQ over traditional approaches",
          "**LINQ API** — Explore the .NET API architecture for LINQ",
          "**LINQ Query Syntax** — Learn the SQL-like query syntax",
          "**LINQ Method Syntax** — Learn the fluent method syntax",
          "**Lambda Expressions** — Understand the building blocks of LINQ methods"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Standard Query Operators"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Master the standard query operators, which are the core methods that make up LINQ:"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Filtering"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "**Where** — Filter elements based on a predicate",
          "**OfType** — Filter elements based on type"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Sorting"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "**OrderBy / OrderByDescending** — Sort elements in ascending or descending order",
          "**ThenBy / ThenByDescending** — Secondary sorting"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Grouping"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "**GroupBy** — Group elements by a key",
          "**ToLookup** — Create a lookup dictionary"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Joining"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "**Join** — Inner join two sequences",
          "**GroupJoin** — Group join (left outer join equivalent)"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Projection"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": ["**Select** — Transform elements", "**SelectMany** — Flatten nested collections"]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Aggregation"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "**Aggregate** — Custom accumulation",
          "**Average** — Calculate average",
          "**Count** — Count elements",
          "**Max** — Find maximum value",
          "**Min** — Find minimum value",
          "**Sum** — Calculate sum"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Quantifiers"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "**All** — Check if all elements satisfy a condition",
          "**Any** — Check if any element satisfies a condition",
          "**Contains** — Check if collection contains a value"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Element Operators"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "**ElementAt / ElementAtOrDefault** — Get element at index",
          "**First / FirstOrDefault** — Get first element",
          "**Last / LastOrDefault** — Get last element",
          "**Single / SingleOrDefault** — Get single element"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Set Operations"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "**Distinct** — Remove duplicates",
          "**Except** — Set difference",
          "**Intersect** — Set intersection",
          "**Union** — Set union"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Partitioning"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": ["**Skip / SkipWhile** — Skip elements", "**Take / TakeWhile** — Take elements"]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Other Operators"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "**Concat** — Concatenate sequences",
          "**SequenceEqual** — Compare sequences for equality",
          "**DefaultIfEmpty** — Handle empty collections",
          "**Empty / Range / Repeat** — Generate collections",
          "**Conversion Operators** — Convert between types"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Advanced Concepts"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "**Expression Trees** — Understand how LINQ providers translate queries",
          "**Deferred Execution** — Learn when queries execute",
          "**Immediate Execution** — Force query execution"
        ]
      }
    },
